    <DataNode elementId="AT1G12010-MONOMER" textLabel="1-aminocyclopropane-1-carboxylate oxidase 3" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT1G12010-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="635" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">This ACO enzyme is one of several Arabidopsis isozymes predicted to catalyzes the last step in ethylene biosynthesis. An aco mutant has ~only 85% of the ethylene present in wild type plants suggesting that this enzyme is active in Arabidopsis seedlings |CITS: [19513806]|.</Comment>
